{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Spectrum","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.ofSlater_via_rank_equality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.ofSlater_via_rank_equality","kind":"def","line":770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L770-L808","doc":"**`SDPSlaterUniqueness` class instance constructor — via\nthe proven rank-equality chain.**\n\nReplaces the dependency on `SDPRankUniqueness` (axiom in\n`SDPRealUniqueness.lean`) with the proven\n`SDPRankUniqueness_proven_via_rank_equality` (this module).\n\nCategorical content is now isolated to:\n* `strict_complementarity_kernel_disjoint` (R2 axiom)\n* `affine_slater_rigidity` (§4.5 axiom)\n\nBoth are atomic Goldman-Tucker statements; replacing them\nwith Mathlib theorems makes the entire chain axiom-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.SDPRankUniqueness_proven_via_rank_equality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.SDPRankUniqueness_proven_via_rank_equality","kind":"theorem","line":729,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L729-L757","doc":"**SDPRankUniqueness from rank equality** —\nclosed proof composing `rank_equality_under_strict_complementarity`\n(proven this module) + `affine_slater_rigidity` (single\ncategorical axiom) + symmetry of the difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.affine_slater_rigidity_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.affine_slater_rigidity_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":700,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L700-L727","doc":"**Active-empty case affine-Slater rigidity** — reduction to\ninterior via `dualSlack = cost`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.affine_slater_rigidity_of_dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.affine_slater_rigidity_of_dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":679,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L679-L698","doc":"**Interior-case affine-Slater rigidity** — proven from\n`Matrix.PosDef` invertibility.  When the dual slack is\nPosDef, `S * D = 0 ⟹ D = 0` directly via `S⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_equality_under_strict_complementarity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_equality_under_strict_complementarity","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L508-L600","doc":"**Rank equality from strict complementarity** —\nproven from kernel disjointness (R2) + range containment\n(R1) + finite-dimensional rank-nullity.\n\nThe proof composes:\n1. range(Φstar) ⊆ ker(S)  (range_contained_in_kernel_of_mul_zero)\n2. ker(Φstar) ∩ ker(S) = {0}  (strict_complementarity_kernel_disjoint)\n3. rank(Φstar) + rank(S) ≤ n  (rank_sum_le_of_mul_zero, proven above)\n4. dim(ker(Φstar)) + dim(ker(S)) ≤ n  (kernel-disjoint ⟹ direct sum)\n5. (n - rank(Φstar)) + (n - rank(S)) ≤ n  (rank-nullity)\n6. ⟹ rank(Φstar) + rank(S) ≥ n\n7. Combined with (3): rank(Φstar) + rank(S) = n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_sum_le_of_mul_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_sum_le_of_mul_zero","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L455-L506","doc":"**Rank inequality from range containment** — proven half:\n`rank(Φstar) + rank(S) ≤ n` (the easy direction).\n\nProof: range(Φstar) ⊆ ker(S) (R1) ⟹ rank(Φstar) ≤\ndim(ker(S)) = n - rank(S).  Pure linear algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_eq_finrank_range_toLin'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.rank_eq_finrank_range_toLin'","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L436-L447","doc":"Standard-basis specialisation of `Matrix.rank_eq_finrank_range_toLin`:\n`M.rank = finrank ℝ (range M.toLin')`.  Since `toLin' = mulVecLin`\n(both send `v ↦ M *ᵥ v`) and `Matrix.rank` is by definition the finrank\nof `range mulVecLin`, the two ranges coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_range_spans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_range_spans","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L346-L427","doc":"**Kernel disjointness from range spanning** — proof\nskeleton via Hermitian inner-product manipulation.\n\nPER COPILOT REVIEW: the proof body still contains 2 small\n`dotProduct_mulVec` adjoint-identity sub-sorries.\nThe structural argument (sum-of-squares zero ⟹ vector is\nzero) is correct; the sub-sorries are mechanical Mathlib\nAPI verifications (likely `dotProduct_mulVec` or\n`Matrix.mulVec_transpose`).  Treated as TODO until Lean\nbuild verifies the exact lemma names.\n\nThe kernel-disjointness `ker(Φ) ∩ ker(S) = {0}` follows from\nthe **range-spanning** hypothesis `range(Φ) + range(S) = ℝ^n`\n(which is the SDP-style strict complementarity statement) via\na clean inner-product argument:\n\nFor `v ∈ ker(Φ) ∩ ker(S)`:\n* Decompose `v = Φ·a + S·b` (range spans ⟹ exists)\n* `⟨v, v⟩ = ⟨v, Φ·a⟩ + ⟨v, S·b⟩`\n* `= ⟨Φᵀ·v, a⟩ + ⟨Sᵀ·v, b⟩`         (adjoint)\n* `= ⟨Φ·v, a⟩ + ⟨S·v, b⟩`           (Hermitian)\n* `= ⟨0, a⟩ + ⟨0, b⟩ = 0`\n* `‖v‖² = 0 ⟹ v = 0`\n\nProof body has 2 small `dotProduct_mulVec` adjoint\nsub-sorries pending Mathlib API name verification.  The\nstructural argument is sound; closure is mechanical once\nthe exact lemma names are confirmed.  This shifts the\ncategorical content from kernel-disjointness to the\n**range-spanning** hypothesis (which is provided explicitly\nwhen needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.range_spans_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.range_spans_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L318-L344","doc":"**Range-spanning when active set is empty + cost PosDef** —\nproven via reduction to the interior case (S = cost\nwhen ystar = 0).  No axiom dependency. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.range_spans_of_dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.range_spans_of_dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L295-L316","doc":"**Range-spanning when dual slack is PosDef** — proven\ndirectly: `S` PosDef ⟹ `range(S) = ℝ^n` ⟹ range-spanning\ntrivial (take a = 0, b = S⁻¹·v).\n\nNo axiom dependency — pure Mathlib `Matrix.PosDef` +\ninvertibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_active_empty_and_cost_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L248-L282","doc":"**Active-empty case kernel disjointness** — proven from\ninterior case via `dualSlack = cost` reduction.\n\nWhen the active set is empty, all dual variables are zero,\nso `dualSlack = cost`.  If the cost is PosDef, we reduce to\nthe interior case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_dualSlack_posDef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.kernel_disjoint_of_dualSlack_posDef","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L218-L246","doc":"**Interior-case kernel disjointness** — proven directly\nfrom `Matrix.PosDef`.\n\nWhen the dual slack `S` is positive-DEFINITE (not just PSD),\nits kernel is trivially `{0}`.  So\n`ker(Φstar) ∩ ker(S) = ker(Φstar) ∩ {0} = {0}` regardless\nof `ker(Φstar)`.\n\nPROOF: PosDef ⟹ `vᵀ S v > 0 for v ≠ 0`.  But `S v = 0` ⟹\n`vᵀ S v = 0`, contradicting strict positivity unless v = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.PosSemidef.rank_via_eigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.PosSemidef.rank_via_eigenvalues","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L156-L184","doc":"**PSD rank via eigenvalues** — for a real PSD matrix, the\nrank equals the count of strictly-positive eigenvalues\n(PSD eigenvalues are non-negative, so equivalently:\nrank = #{i : eigenvalues i ≠ 0}).\n\n**Status: PROVEN** (de-axiomatised) — composes the proven\nhelper `eigenvalues_pos_filter_eq_ne_zero_filter` (PSD\neigenvalues are `≥ 0`, so `> 0` ⟺ `≠ 0`) with Mathlib's\n`Matrix.IsHermitian.rank_eq_card_non_zero_eigs`\n(`rank A = #{i // eigenvalues i ≠ 0}`, immediate from the\nspectral theorem) and `Fintype.card_subtype` (bridging the\nsubtype-card to the `Finset.filter` card).\n\nRef: [boyd-vandenberghe-2004] *Convex Optimization* §A.5.5\n(rank of a Hermitian matrix equals the number of non-zero\neigenvalues; immediate from the spectral theorem). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.PosSemidef.eigenvalues_pos_filter_eq_ne_zero_filter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRankEquality.PosSemidef.eigenvalues_pos_filter_eq_ne_zero_filter","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPRankEquality.lean#L138-L154","doc":"**PSD eigenvalue filter equivalence** — for a PSD matrix,\n\"strictly positive eigenvalue\" coincides with \"non-zero\neigenvalue\" (since PSD eigenvalues are non-negative).\nFully proven; no Mathlib gap. ","signatureChunk":0}]}